<hr data-start=3D"1804" data-end=3D"1807">
<h2 data-start=3D"1809" data-end=3D"1864">=E2=9D=97 Important =E2=80=94 Whe=
n CDS returns ZIP instead of NetCDF</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1866" data-end=3D"1895">There are only <strong data-start=
=3D"1881" data-end=3D"1894">3 reasons</strong>:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1897" data-end=3D"1954">=E2=9D=8C 1. Wrong API key =E2=86=
=92 CDS returns an HTML error page</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1955" data-end=3D"1983">=E2=86=92 Browser-like ZIP contain=
er</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1985" data-end=3D"2041">=E2=9D=8C 2. Wrong product =E2=86=
=92 CDS returns compressed bundle</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2042" data-end=3D"2096">(e.g., if dataset ID is misspelled=
, CDS zips an error)</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2098" data-end=3D"2152">=E2=9D=8C 3. Cloudflare or proxy =
intercepted the request</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2153" data-end=3D"2184">=E2=86=92 returning ZIP-wrapped co=
ntent</p>
<p data-start=3D"2186" data-end=3D"2223">We can detect which one is happeni=
ng.</p>
