<p data-start=3D"1535" data-end=3D"1670">(Shell tip: you can just list mult=
iple patterns, or put them all in one directory and filter by year in scrip=
t if you want it cleaner.)</p>
<p data-start=3D"1672" data-end=3D"1677">This:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1679" data-end=3D"1838">
<li data-start=3D"1679" data-end=3D"1721">
<p data-start=3D"1681" data-end=3D"1721">Cuts data size by ~30=E2=80=9340% =
vs 2020=E2=80=932025</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1722" data-end=3D"1789">
<p data-start=3D"1724" data-end=3D"1789">Still covers recent years (COVID/p=
ost-COVID, recent ENSO, etc.)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1790" data-end=3D"1838">
<p data-start=3D"1792" data-end=3D"1838">Keeps training time manageable on =
rented GPU</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1840" data-end=3D"1888">=F0=9F=94=B9 Phase 2 =E2=80=93 If=
 you want more accuracy later</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1890" data-end=3D"1923">Once miner is running and stable:<=
/p>
<ul data-start=3D"1925" data-end=3D"2057">
<li data-start=3D"1925" data-end=3D"1994">
<p data-start=3D"1927" data-end=3D"1994">Re-train with <strong data-start=
=3D"1941" data-end=3D"1954">2020=E2=80=932025</strong> if you want to squee=
ze more performance</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1995" data-end=3D"2057">
<p data-start=3D"1997" data-end=3D"2057">Or only for the =E2=80=9Chard=E2=
=80=9D variable like <strong data-start=3D"2034" data-end=3D"2057">total_pr=
ecipitation</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2059" data-end=3D"2125">You don=E2=80=99t need to do that =
before your miner is online and earning.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2127" data-end=3D"2130">
<h2 data-start=3D"2132" data-end=3D"2170">4=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 So, should yo=
u <em data-start=3D"2154" data-end=3D"2161">start</em> at 2020?</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"2172" data-end=3D"2389">
<li data-start=3D"2172" data-end=3D"2246">
<p data-start=3D"2174" data-end=3D"2246"><strong data-start=3D"2174" data-e=
nd=3D"2207">For long-term =E2=80=9Cfinal=E2=80=9D models:</strong><br data-=
start=3D"2207" data-end=3D"2210">
=E2=9C=85 Yes, 2020=E2=80=93now is a great window.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2248" data-end=3D"2389">
<p data-start=3D"2250" data-end=3D"2389"><strong data-start=3D"2250" data-e=
nd=3D"2304">For first working version (to get off -36% score):</strong><br =
data-start=3D"2304" data-end=3D"2307">
=F0=9F=94=A5 I=E2=80=99d start from <strong data-start=3D"2327" data-end=3D=
"2335">2022</strong> or even <strong data-start=3D"2344" data-end=3D"2352">=
2023</strong>, get something running, then expand.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2391" data-end=3D"2456">Think of 2020=E2=80=932021 as =E2=
=80=9Cextra training spice=E2=80=9D, not mandatory core.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2458" data-end=3D"2461">
<p data-start=3D"2463" data-end=3D"2566">If you tell me <strong data-start=
=3D"2478" data-end=3D"2507">what GPU you plan to rent</strong> (e.g. A10G 2=
4GB, L4 24GB, 3090 24GB, etc.), I can suggest:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2568" data-end=3D"2661">
<li data-start=3D"2568" data-end=3D"2580">
<p data-start=3D"2570" data-end=3D"2580">batch size</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2581" data-end=3D"2589">
<p data-start=3D"2583" data-end=3D"2589">epochs</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2590" data-end=3D"2661">
<p data-start=3D"2592" data-end=3D"2661">how many years to use per training=
