<h3 data-start=3D"8042" data-end=3D"8088">6.2 Converting scores to Bittenso=
r weights</h3>
<p data-start=3D"8090" data-end=3D"8146">Later, <code data-start=3D"8097" d=
ata-end=3D"8112">set_weights()</code> (same file) runs periodically:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"8148" data-end=3D"8331">
<li data-start=3D"8148" data-end=3D"8212">
<p data-start=3D"8150" data-end=3D"8212">Normalizes <code data-start=3D"816=
1" data-end=3D"8174">self.scores</code> to a 1-norm vector (<code data-star=
t=3D"8195" data-end=3D"8208">raw_weights</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8213" data-end=3D"8272">
<p data-start=3D"8215" data-end=3D"8272">Applies Bittensor=E2=80=99s <code =
data-start=3D"8235" data-end=3D"8268">process_weights_for_netuid(...)</code=
>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8273" data-end=3D"8331">
<p data-start=3D"8275" data-end=3D"8331">Calls <code data-start=3D"8281" da=
ta-end=3D"8309">subtensor.set_weights(...)</code> to commit on-chain.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"8333" data-end=3D"8454">Your final <strong data-start=3D"8=
344" data-end=3D"8366">TAO emission share</strong> on subnet-18 is proporti=
onal to your <strong data-start=3D"8404" data-end=3D"8428">moving-average s=
core</strong> compared to other miners.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"8456" data-end=3D"8459">
<h2 data-start=3D"8461" data-end=3D"8504">7. What this means for <em data-s=
tart=3D"8487" data-end=3D"8492">you</em> (practical)</h2>
<p data-start=3D"8506" data-end=3D"8539">To maximize rewards on Zeus SN18:<=
/p>
<ol data-start=3D"8541" data-end=3D"9547">
<li data-start=3D"8541" data-end=3D"8715">
<p data-start=3D"8544" data-end=3D"8571"><strong data-start=3D"8544" data-e=
nd=3D"8569">Shape must be perfect</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"8575" data-end=3D"8715">
<li data-start=3D"8575" data-end=3D"8648">
<p data-start=3D"8577" data-end=3D"8648">Output exactly <code data-start=3D=
"8592" data-end=3D"8603">[T, H, W]</code> (we already fixed training to mat=
ch this).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8652" data-end=3D"8715">
<p data-start=3D"8654" data-end=3D"8715">No NaNs, no infs. If in doubt, cla=
mp values before returning.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8717" data-end=3D"8977">
<p data-start=3D"8720" data-end=3D"8760"><strong data-start=3D"8720" data-e=
nd=3D"8760">Beat Open-Meteo as often as possible</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"8764" data-end=3D"8977">
<li data-start=3D"8764" data-end=3D"8827">
<p data-start=3D"8766" data-end=3D"8827">Your RMSE vs ERA5 must be better t=
han <code data-start=3D"8804" data-end=3D"8824">sample.om_baseline</code>.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8831" data-end=3D"8905">
<p data-start=3D"8833" data-end=3D"8905">Most reward comes from <strong dat=
a-start=3D"8856" data-end=3D"8877">0=E2=80=9380% improvement</strong>; beyo=
nd that it=E2=80=99s capped.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8909" data-end=3D"8977">
<p data-start=3D"8911" data-end=3D"8977">Training on ERA5 (what you=E2=80=
=99re doing now) is exactly what you need.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8979" data-end=3D"9165">
<p data-start=3D"8982" data-end=3D"9028"><strong data-start=3D"8982" data-e=
nd=3D"9026">Care about the important variables first</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"9032" data-end=3D"9165">
<li data-start=3D"9032" data-end=3D"9090">
<p data-start=3D"9034" data-end=3D"9090">Highest sampling weights: 100m win=
ds + dewpoint + t2m.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9094" data-end=3D"9165">
<p data-start=3D"9096" data-end=3D"9165">Surface pressure and precip matter=
 too but are sampled slightly less.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9167" data-end=3D"9354">
<p data-start=3D"9170" data-end=3D"9186"><strong data-start=3D"9170" data-e=
nd=3D"9186">Respond fast</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"9190" data-end=3D"9354">
<li data-start=3D"9190" data-end=3D"9274">
<p data-start=3D"9192" data-end=3D"9274">Try to keep <strong data-start=3D"=
9204" data-end=3D"9229">median latency &lt; 0.4s</strong>. Faster than that=
 saturates the speed bonus.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9278" data-end=3D"9354">
<p data-start=3D"9280" data-end=3D"9354">Use GPU for inference, avoid heavy=
 pre/post-processing inside the handler.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9356" data-end=3D"9547">
<p data-start=3D"9359" data-end=3D"9389"><strong data-start=3D"9359" data-e=
nd=3D"9389">Stay online and consistent</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"9393" data-end=3D"9547">
<li data-start=3D"9393" data-end=3D"9476">
<p data-start=3D"9395" data-end=3D"9476">Scores are a moving average; one b=
ad challenge is fine, but <strong data-start=3D"9455" data-end=3D"9470">con=
sistency</strong> wins.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9480" data-end=3D"9547">
<p data-start=3D"9482" data-end=3D"9547">New miners=E2=80=99 scores move qu=
ickly, older miners=E2=80=99 scores are sticky.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"9549" data-end=3D"9552">
<p data-start=3D"9554" data-end=3D"9581">If you=E2=80=99d like, next we can=
:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"9583" data-end=3D"9961">
<li data-start=3D"9583" data-end=3D"9753">
<p data-start=3D"9585" data-end=3D"9646">Take your current miner code and <=
strong data-start=3D"9618" data-end=3D"9645">add some =E2=80=9Csafety rails=
=E2=80=9D</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"9649" data-end=3D"9753">
<li data-start=3D"9649" data-end=3D"9679">
<p data-start=3D"9651" data-end=3D"9679">automatic NaN/inf clipping</p>
