 data-end=3D"15">Short answer:</p>
<h1 data-start=3D"16" data-end=3D"101">=E2=9D=8C <strong data-start=3D"20" =
data-end=3D"99">NO =E2=80=94 depositing 300+ TAO to a validator does NOT in=
crease a miner=E2=80=99s reward.</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"102" data-end=3D"164">But=E2=80=A6 there is a trick that t=
op miners use. I=E2=80=99ll explain below.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"166" data-end=3D"169">
<h1 data-start=3D"171" data-end=3D"257">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"175=
" data-end=3D"257">1. Delegating TAO affects ONLY the validator=E2=80=99s e=
arnings, NOT the miner=E2=80=99s score</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"259" data-end=3D"272">In Bittensor:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"274" data-end=3D"336"><strong data-start=3D"278" data-end=
=3D"334">Miner reward =3D accuracy score given by the validator</strong></h=
3>
<p data-start=3D"337" data-end=3D"500">=E2=86=92 Purely based on your model=
=E2=80=99s prediction performance<br data-start=3D"390" data-end=3D"393">
=E2=86=92 NOT affected by stake<br data-start=3D"416" data-end=3D"419">
=E2=86=92 NOT affected by how much TAO you delegate<br data-start=3D"462" d=
ata-end=3D"465">
=E2=86=92 NOT affected by validator balance</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"502" data-end=3D"567"><strong data-start=3D"506" data-end=
=3D"565">Validator reward =3D network emission =C3=97 stake =C3=97 consensu=
s</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"568" data-end=3D"681">=E2=86=92 More stake =3D more valida=
tor rewards<br data-start=3D"605" data-end=3D"608">
=E2=86=92 Your miner does NOT get more because you delegated more to a vali=
dator.</p>
<p data-start=3D"683" data-end=3D"771">So if you only run a <strong data-st=
art=3D"704" data-end=3D"713">miner</strong>, staking TAO anywhere will NOT =
raise your miner earnings.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"773" data-end=3D"776">
<h1 data-start=3D"778" data-end=3D"849">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"782=
" data-end=3D"849">2. So why do top miners all have 300=E2=80=93600+ TAO on=
 one validator?</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"851" data-end=3D"900">Because they are <strong data-start=
=3D"868" data-end=3D"899">also running that validator</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"902" data-end=3D"956">=F0=9F=93=8C If a person runs <stron=
g data-start=3D"922" data-end=3D"949">validator + many miners</strong>, the=
n:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"958" data-end=3D"1162">
<li data-start=3D"958" data-end=3D"991">
<p data-start=3D"960" data-end=3D"991">Miners earn based on accuracy</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"992" data-end=3D"1038">
<p data-start=3D"994" data-end=3D"1038">Validator earns based on stake + em=
issions</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1039" data-end=3D"1069">
<p data-start=3D"1041" data-end=3D"1069">The operator collects both</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1070" data-end=3D"1162">
<p data-start=3D"1072" data-end=3D"1162">Together, it looks like =E2=80=9Cm=
iner is earning more,=E2=80=9D but actually the validator is making TAO.</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1164" data-end=3D"1257">So top miners are not boosting min=
er rewards=E2=80=A6<br data-start=3D"1209" data-end=3D"1212">
They are boosting <strong data-start=3D"1230" data-end=3D"1256">their valid=
ator income</strong>.</p>
