<h1 data-start=3D"1264" data-end=3D"1347">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"1=
268" data-end=3D"1347">3. Does a validator with more stake give =E2=80=9Cbe=
tter scores=E2=80=9D to its own miners?</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"1349" data-end=3D"1364">No. Impossible.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1366" data-end=3D"1600">
<li data-start=3D"1366" data-end=3D"1422">
<p data-start=3D"1368" data-end=3D"1422">Validators cannot recognize miners=
 by IP or identity</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1423" data-end=3D"1462">
<p data-start=3D"1425" data-end=3D"1462">Scores must follow the subnet logi=
c</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1463" data-end=3D"1525">
<p data-start=3D"1465" data-end=3D"1525">If a validator cheats, the network=
 punishes it (consensus)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1526" data-end=3D"1600">
<p data-start=3D"1528" data-end=3D"1600">Validator cannot =E2=80=9Cboost=E2=
=80=9D its own miners without harming its own emission</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1602" data-end=3D"1662">So:<br data-start=3D"1605" data-en=
d=3D"1608">
<strong data-start=3D"1608" data-end=3D"1662">Stake on validator does NOT c=
ontrol miner ranking.</strong></p>
